  "articleBody": "Adjustable showerheads are fantastic because they let you customize your showering experience, but getting that 'perfect spray' means a good installation and understanding your unit. It all starts with compatibility. You’ll want to make sure your new adjustable showerhead works with your current shower arm. Most customer questions revolve around this, plus how many spray settings there are and whether you need tape or washers. The basic installation process is pretty straightforward: first, remove your old showerhead, then give those threads a good clean. Next, apply the sealing method recommended by the manufacturer – don't guess here, as some need tape, some just washers, and some are designed for hand-tightening only. Screw on your new adjustable head or its connector, and then the crucial step: test every single spray setting and check for any leaks. You really want to make sure it's all sealed up and performing as it should. If you find yourself with persistent leaks, especially if there's also low flow or you're dealing with a complex setup involving a wall-mounted bracket or specific backflow prevention requirements, it’s definitely wise to bring in an expert. HH Remodeling LLC can ensure your adjustable showerhead is installed flawlessly, so you can enjoy every spray.",
